======================================================================================================================
G5 (iii) B3's onset gate: DE12/DE13 structural statement (a smooth on/off gate flat at both ends has W'' of both signs), sympy
======================================================================================================================
  W(u) = -2*u**3 + 3*u**2; W'(0) = 0, W'(1) = 0; W'' = 6 - 12*u (>0 on u < 1/2, <0 on u > 1/2)
  a smooth gate flat at both ends therefore has a wrong-sign second variation on half of every transition layer [R: DE12/DE13; CFG172 sec. 0.5]. B3's onset gate is a SHARP mask (an unvaried mask, the V0 obstruction): stable only because nothing varies it; varied as a term it meets this statement. Scored as a statement.
  [PASS] gate statement: the smoothstep W has W'(0) = W'(1) = 0 and W'' of both signs (the DE12 structure), sympy
         W'' = 6 - 12*u

======================================================================================================================
G5 (iv) c_T = c and gamma (statements)
======================================================================================================================
  c_T = c: the class-V action is minimally coupled (no A^mu A^nu R_mu nu, no xi R A^2): the tensor sector is GR's, c_T = 1 [H, statement; P]. Non-minimal couplings are NOT covered.
  gamma: the drag force acts on baryons as a potential force and leaves the metric unmodified at this order: gamma - 1 = 0 (Cassini P) [H, statement]; but the SAME statement means the vector force does not deflect light (lensing versus dynamics, diagnostic D2: not scored).
  ghost: A3.1-A3.2 show that the attractive drag needs s = -1 (a ghost) for V0, V1 (K1, K2, K3); V2's dark mass is negative (A3.4).

